To add a newsletter sign-up form to your website, here is a clean, modern, and mobile-responsive code snippet using **HTML and CSS**.

### 1. HTML
Paste this code where you want the sign-up form to appear on your page:

```html
<div class="newsletter-container">
  <div class="newsletter-content">
    <h2>Subscribe to our newsletter</h2>
    <p>Get the latest news, updates, and special offers delivered directly to your inbox.</p>

    <form class="newsletter-form" action="#" method="POST">
      <input 
        type="email" 
        name="email" 
        placeholder="Enter your email address" 
        required 
        aria-label="Email address"
      />
      <button type="submit">Subscribe</button>
    </form>

    <p class="privacy-notice">We respect your privacy. Unsubscribe at any time.</p>
  </div>
</div>
```

---

### 2. CSS
Add this to your stylesheet (e.g., `style.css`) or inside a `<style>` tag in your `<head>`:

```css
.newsletter-container {
  background-color: #f8fafc;
  border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 40px 20px;
  max-width: 600px;
  margin: 40px auto;
  text-align: center;
  font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
}

.newsletter-content h2 {
  font-size: 24px;
  color: #1e293b;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
}

.newsletter-content p {
  font-size: 15px;
  color: #64748b;
  margin-bottom: 24px;
}

.newsletter-form {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 10px;
  max-width: 450px;
  margin: 0 auto;
}

.newsletter-form input[type="email"] {
  padding: 12px 16px;
  border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
  border-radius: 6px;
  font-size: 15px;
  outline: none;
  transition: border-color 0.2s;
}

.newsletter-form input[type="email"]:focus {
  border-color: #3b82f6;
}

.newsletter-form button {
  padding: 12px 24px;
  background-color: #2563eb;
  color: #ffffff;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 6px;
  font-size: 15px;
  font-weight: 600;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background-color 0.2s;
}

.newsletter-form button:hover {
  background-color: #1d4ed8;
}

.newsletter-content .privacy-notice {
  font-size: 12px;
  color: #94a3b8;
  margin-top: 16px;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

/* Side-by-side layout for desktop screens */
@media (min-width: 480px) {
  .newsletter-form {
    flex-direction: row;
  }

  .newsletter-form input[type="email"] {
    flex: 1;
  }
}
```

---

### Next Step: Connecting It to an Email Service
Right now, the form has `action="#"`, which means it won't actually store the email anywhere. 

To collect emails, you need to connect it to a provider. Tell me which platform you use, and I can give you the exact integration code:
* **Email Service:** Mailchimp, ConvertKit, Brevo, Substack, Buttondown, or Klaviyo?
* **Website Builder/CMS:** WordPress, Shopify, Webflow, Squarespace, or raw HTML/React?

